WEBVTT

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:07.940
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:42.930
<i>Target distance: 5 nautical miles.</i> <i>Cyclops team, are you ready?</i>

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.060
<i>Ready to launch.</i>

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:46.100
<i>All hatches, flooded.</i>

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.940
<i>Crack seals on hatches</i> <i>2, 4, 1, and 3.</i>

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.820
<i>Cyclops team... LAUNCH!</i>

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>All units, maintain depth at 1-5-0</i> <i>and proceed towards target area.</i>

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.340
<i>Roger.</i>

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:19.640
We're 15 minutes behind schedule. All units, increase speed to 30.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:22.560
<i>We'll land at 15:00</i> <i>hours, as planned.</i>

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.190
<i>Report says the beach'll be foggy,</i> <i>temperature's 12 below.</i>

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:30.400
<i>Misha, you can warm up, but</i> <i>don't go nuts with the booze.</i>

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.610
I'm reading a warm current flowing from the iceberg in front of us.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.530
It's an undersea passage. It might lead into the base.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.910
Garcia! Misha! Proceed on course, as planned.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.950
<i>Andy and I will go in</i> <i>through the passage.</i>

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:44.120
<i>Roger.</i>

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:43.810
We're under attack by two Gogg-type mobile suits!

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.930
Brown team, scramble and form a defense line!

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:48.390
Transport team, get those containers loaded, fast!

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:49.810
There's two more left. Even if we hurry...

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:51.810
...we'll need 10 minutes to get them stowed!

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.770
<i>- You've got 5 minutes!</i>
- Get real!

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:39.490
Captain, I don't see it in the transport plane.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.990
<i>Same story in the hangar.</i>

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:43.740
<i>I think these ground</i> <i>targets are all decoys.</i>

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:45.950
Andy, what's happening on your end?

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>I'm on a lift,</i> <i>approaching the exit.</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.870
<i>Check it out, just</i> <i>watch your step.</i>

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:51.040
<i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:02.260
<i>Captain, they've got a shuttle</i> <i>getting ready to launch!</i>

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.890
<i>It may be in the containers</i> <i>they're loading onto it!</i>

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.550
<i>Can you give me a visual?</i>

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:07.010
<i>Just a still.</i>

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.310
Doesn't matter.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.100
Keep it from launching!

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:14.480
You're authorized to use your missile!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.650
<i>Aye, sir!</i>

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.570
<i>They've got a GM covering it!</i>
<i>I'm pinned down!</i>

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.400
<i>They're gonna get away!</i>

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.160
<i>Hold on,</i> <i>I'm coming to help you!</i>

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:26.570
They've already started the countdown! You'll never make it!

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:27.740
I'm going for it!

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.410
<i>Andy, wait!</i>

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:37.340
ANDY!!!

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:41.820
How Many Miles to the Battlefield?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:50.160
<i>Can't you see that you are sweet?</i>

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:57.750
<i>Oh, let me love you so.</i>

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:13.850
<i>As I look up, the sky above seems so far away...</i>

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:13.850
<i><i>miageru sora wa tooi kedo</i></i>

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:20.020
<i>...but there are dreams that even it can't hold.</i>

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:20.020
<i>kakae kirenai yume ga aru</i>

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:30.990
<i>Oh, yes, I want to slip away from this artificial world...</i>

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:30.990
<i>sou yo, tsukurareta sekai no naka wo mukidashite</i>

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>...and make myself free.</i>

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:35.370
<i>jiyuu ni naritai</i>

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:49.590
<i>I can keep on running till I finally reach the sky.</i>

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:49.590
<i>hashi ni tsuzukete sora ni todoteba</i>

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:59.980
<i>Since I can believe that I can become the wind someday...</i>

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:59.980
<i>kaze ni nareru to sou shinjiteru kara</i>

00:07:00.020 --> 00:07:06.150
<i>I never give up forever.</i>

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.430
Al, come on! It's hamburger today.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:34.180
Aw, it's just synth-meat again.

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.100
Third time this month. I'm getting sick of it.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.640
Oh, come on, complaining won't make it taste any better.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.900
I wish I was like you. You can eat anything.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:48.650
My mom says we have less stuff now because of the war.

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.400
The war's with the Zeon and the Federation.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.610
It doesn't have anything to do with this colony!

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:57.030
It holds the supply ships up sometimes.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:00.960
I'll eat those if you don't want them.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.670
I've got something really cool to show you...

00:08:11.920 --> 00:08:16.100
A Federal Forces rank badge. A real one!

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:19.100
- Can I hold it?
- Just for a little while.

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.980
My big brother's a mobile suit pilot.

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:24.900
He gave it to you?

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:26.860
Uh-huh, and it was a lot of trouble, too.

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:30.280
Cool! A Fed pilot!

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.610
He's making it up.

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:35.570
The Federation doesn't even HAVE any mobile suits!

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:40.620
Girls don't know anything.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.660
Aw, she's just stupid.

00:08:42.750 --> 00:08:46.330
The Federation has mobile suits. Don't be such a know-it-all!

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:52.090
They do NOT have mobile suits!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:54.760
They didn't before, but they do now.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.300
You're just making it up!

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.760
Chay's right! I've seen their mobile suits!

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.810
My dad works in a shipping company, right?

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:07.100
He showed me one in the space port.

00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:10.320
It was a mobile suit being shipped over to Side 7.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.400
You're making it up.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:17.700
That mobile suit was big and black. It looked really tough!

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:18.950
Where's your proof?

00:09:18.990 --> 00:09:20.530
Proof?

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:27.500
You're making it all up. I'll bet that rank badge is a fake, too!

00:09:27.750 --> 00:09:28.880
What?!

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.170
What are you doing?!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.670
Why, you...

00:09:37.760 --> 00:09:38.800
You shrimp!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:39.890
Frog-face!

00:09:43.140 --> 00:09:44.810
What a jerk!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:47.850
Yeah, they don't come much worse than her.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.060
I'd sure like to show her!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:53.730
Get real. She'd probably talk you to death.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:56.030
All we need is some proof.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:09:58.700
A snapshot or a video of a mobile suit...

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.370
Hey, Al! Didn't you say you were meeting your dad today?

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.420
I'm home!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:18.930
Welcome back.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.150
Weren't you going straight over to the space port?

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:37.440
I forgot something. Bye, Mom!

00:10:41.990 --> 00:10:44.990
<i>Just get a picture of a Fed</i> <i>mobile suit at the space port.</i>

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:49.750
<i>That'll be our proof! Do it,</i> <i>and I'll give you the rank badge.</i>

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:09.350
Alfred Izuruha. Age: 11. Code number 0039295 MC.

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:16.860
Okay, there you go. Your daddy's ship will be coming in at gate 23.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:20.030
Should be docked in about 10 minutes.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:20.910
Thanks.

00:12:11.870 --> 00:12:15.670
Darn it, there's nothing in here that even looks like a mobile suit.

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:24.970
You there! What are you doing in here?

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.140
I'm just looking for a restroom. Is there one in here?

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.180
Go out to the hallway near the lifts. Third door.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:33.730
Thanks, mister.

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:35.900
Don't wet yourself!

00:12:35.980 --> 00:12:39.400
What's going on? Anything wrong up there?

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.650
A kid wandered in, that's all. Relax!

00:12:43.280 --> 00:12:45.490
Okay, let's get going on the inspection!

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:04.630
What's wrong? You're so quiet today.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:07.430
Is Mother well?

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:08.720
So-so.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:09.970
So-so?

00:13:10.010 --> 00:13:12.980
Okay, I guess. Same as usual.

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:16.400
I see... Well, how were your tests?

00:13:16.440 --> 00:13:18.230
You had your achievements on the 3rd, right?

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.730
So-so.

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:22.280
What's the overall average?

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:23.440
C minus.

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.950
How about in math and science?

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:27.200
A minus and B plus.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.080
Yeah, you're pretty sharp in science.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:33.370
Oh, yes, could you give this to Mother for me?

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.000
That's an important letter, so don't lose it.

00:13:40.090 --> 00:13:42.590
Dad, can you do me a favor?

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:29.180
Oh, I'm sorry! Are you all right?!

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:31.470
You aren't hurt, are you?

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:34.350
Oh, no! The end of your nose is turning all red and...

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:36.850
Al? Al, it's you!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:42.440
I'm Christina Mackenzie. Chris.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:47.400
You don't remember me?

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:50.820
No, I remember you, Chris...

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.870
You went to Earth! When'd you get back?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:58.830
This afternoon. I was just carrying my stuff into my room and...

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:03.960
Oh, no! Everything's getting soaked!

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:05.380
I'll help you.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:06.840
The stuff in the car.

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.840
Get the bag on the passenger side and the papers, too.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.470
Okay.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.560
A government job?

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:26.570
I was sent up here on really short notice, so it's been crazy.

00:15:26.610 --> 00:15:29.400
Even had to get my Mom to take care of the red tape for me.

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:33.070
Just a sec.

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:46.550
Mom isn't here, and I don't know where Dad's clothes are.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:48.590
This'll just have to do.

00:15:54.220 --> 00:15:57.100
Al, do you like milk tea?

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:58.350
Fine with me.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:05.360
There you go. Tell me if it needs more sugar.

00:16:09.320 --> 00:16:10.360
It's great.

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:31.630
If you were going to be late, you should've told me sooner!

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:36.140
I was worried you'd gotten into an accident or something!

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.680
Thanks for the food.

00:16:41.310 --> 00:16:44.060
Is your father the same?

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:47.310
I see...

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:53.570
He gave me that envelope to give to you. He said it's a letter.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:03.540
I'm done.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:05.000
You've hardly eaten any!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.960
I ate with Dad, so I'm not that hungry now.

00:17:07.960 --> 00:17:11.170
Well, if you get hungry later on, don't come running to me!

00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.200
Al?

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.910
Just a sec. I'll unlock it.

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.750
You've got phys-ed tomorrow, right?

00:17:49.790 --> 00:17:52.550
Put this in your bag before you forget it.

00:17:52.590 --> 00:17:53.920
Yes, Mom.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.920
And go straight to bed after you've finished your homework.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:56.720
Yes, Mom.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.300
You're just full of the right answers today.

00:17:58.340 --> 00:17:59.800
Yes, Mom.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.350
Yes, Mom.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:06.180
Yes, Mom.

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:08.560
Yes, Mom.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.270
Yes, Mom.

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:11.440
Yes, Mom.

00:18:11.480 --> 00:18:12.570
Yes, Mom.

00:18:12.610 --> 00:18:13.730
Yes, Mom.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:14.740
Yes, Mom.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.740
Yes, Mom.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:16.320
Yes, Mom.

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.490
BANG!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:08.210
Hey, candid cameraman! How are you feeling this morning?

00:19:09.410 --> 00:19:11.710
Not bad!

00:19:11.750 --> 00:19:13.540
Is school really that boring?

00:19:13.590 --> 00:19:15.090
It sucks!

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:19.590
My homeroom teacher's boring, gives us lots of homework...

00:19:19.630 --> 00:19:21.720
...and she makes me stand in the corner all the time!

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:23.550
Do you have to do that a lot?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:25.100
Once in a while.

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:28.770
The food stinks, and so does having to clean the toilets.

00:19:28.810 --> 00:19:30.770
And there's this girl there I can't stand!

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.730
AND I have to go there for a whole other year!

00:19:33.770 --> 00:19:35.980
There's still junior high and high school.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.440
Who knows what THAT'S gonna be like.

00:19:39.990 --> 00:19:41.570
See you!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.750
I asked my dad and he let me in.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:54.250
But there weren't any Fed ships there yesterday.

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.670
Just commercial ships.

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.710
Yeah, all you got were shots of these containers.

00:19:59.840 --> 00:20:02.340
Looks like I get to keep my rank badge.

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:03.840
Oh, well...

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.220
You really want that junk that bad?

00:20:06.890 --> 00:20:08.430
Rear admiral, fleet admiral, petty officer...

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.230
...corporal, department head, section chief.

00:20:10.270 --> 00:20:12.600
There's a toy store near here selling them for 1 kule each.

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:16.150
You guys are really stupid, getting excited over this junk.

00:20:16.190 --> 00:20:18.110
Shut up!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:27.240
Over there!

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:30.080
A Federation mobile suit!

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.200
It's Zeon!

00:20:45.010 --> 00:20:46.050
Run!

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:05.910
COOL!

00:21:05.990 --> 00:21:08.070
This is better than fireworks!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.080
Another one's coming down!

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.120
A Zaku! It's hit.

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:14.710
It's coming towards us. It's gonna crash!

00:21:38.900 --> 00:21:40.400
It's going down.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:42.530
Looks like it's heading west.

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:46.240
Might be trying for Forest Park... Hey, Al, what gives?

00:21:46.280 --> 00:21:48.450
Are you cutting class?

00:23:06.570 --> 00:23:08.780
<i>It's still hot.</i>

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:20.200
<i>On that night I told them that lie...</i>

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:20.200
<i>uso wo tsuita yoru ni wa</i>

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:26.930
<i>...I couldn't sleep. That's how scared I was.</i>

00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:26.930
<i>nemurezu ni kowakatta</i>

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:33.340
<i>But no matter how bad of a fight we would have...</i>

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:33.340
<i>donna kenka wo shite mo</i>

00:24:33.640 --> 00:24:40.210
<i>...by the next day, it would be forgotten.</i>

00:24:33.640 --> 00:24:40.210
<i>tsugi no hi wa wasureteita</i>

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:47.690
<i>The sky would be so blue...</i>

00:24:42.510 --> 00:24:47.690
<i>sora ga aoi koto</i>

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:55.030
<i>...and that would make me so glad.</i>

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:55.030
<i>sore ga ureshikute</i>

00:24:55.660 --> 00:25:01.540
<i>There would be times when I'd doubt others...</i>

00:24:55.660 --> 00:25:01.540
<i>itsuka hito wo utagai</i>

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:08.480
<i>...and I'd know the loneliness of living.</i>

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:08.480
<i>ikiru sabishisa shiru koto mo</i>

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:14.540
<i>But that was something I didn't notice then.</i>

00:25:08.540 --> 00:25:14.540
<i>ki ga tsukazu ni subete wo</i>

00:25:14.940 --> 00:25:19.980
<i>Back when I believed in everything...</i>

00:25:14.940 --> 00:25:19.980
<i>shinjiteta koro</i>

00:25:43.730 --> 00:25:45.730
NEXT EPISODE

00:25:45.890 --> 00:25:48.400
Give it back! Give it back!

00:25:48.440 --> 00:25:50.060
Why, you...

00:25:51.570 --> 00:25:53.030
Darn you!

00:25:53.150 --> 00:25:54.740
OW!

00:25:54.740 --> 00:25:56.910
Receiver's credentials?

00:25:56.910 --> 00:25:59.870
Oh, a secret mission, huh?

00:25:59.870 --> 00:26:01.780
Well, the truth is...

00:26:01.830 --> 00:26:04.450
A Newtype-use Gundam, you think?

00:26:09.750 --> 00:26:11.750
WAR IN THE POCKET

00:26:11.750 --> 00:26:13.760
Episode 2 Reflections in a Brown Eye
